lawful order of a university agent that I am required to obey.

There are two cases:
   1) the "offender" *is not* violating the university sexual
      harassment policy. In this case, the sys admin has no grounds to
      request/order me to cease and desist.
   2) the "offender" *is* violating the univeristy sexual harasssment
      policy. In this case, the sys admin is not one of the folk
      authorized to enforce the policy, and so has no grounds to
      request/order me to cease and desist.

Notice that it in either case it is not necessary for the sys admin to
judge if the complaint is valid.

So what should a sys admin do?

========================= (from the report) ==========
    1. Tell the alleged offender, "A complaint has been made about an
       image/sound emanating from your workstation."

    2. Give the alleged offender a copy of the Brochure on the
       University Sexual Harassment Policy (enclosed; call 333-9183 to
       request additional notices or brochures).

    3. Make a note of the following, and return it to the system
       administrator:
              o Date, time, and place of alleged offense. 
              o Identity of the accused and accuser.
              o Nature of the alleged offense.
       This information must be kept confidential and retained for use
       if a formal complaint is lodged against the alleged offender.
==================

Thus the sys admin shares information and documents the facts, but he
or she should not interpret or enforce the sexual harassment policy.

